tion to this plan?","enroll_form.address.city":"City","enroll_form.address.city.error":"Enter your city.","enroll_form.address.line_1":"Address line 1","enroll_form.address.line_1.error":"Enter your address.","enroll_form.address.phone.error":"Enter a phone number.","enroll_form.address.state":"State","enroll_form.address.state.error":"Enter your state.","enroll_form.address.zip":"ZIP code","enroll_form.address.zip.error":"Enter your 5-digit ZIP code.","enroll_form.address_line_1":"Address line 1","enroll_form.address_line_2":"Address line 2","enroll_form.agreement.by_completing_enrollment_agree_to_following":"By completing this enrollment application, I agree to the following:","enroll_form.agreement.chosen_to_enroll_in_plan":"You have chosen to enroll in {plan_name}","enroll_form.agreement.click_box_to_continue":"Click the box to continue.","enroll_form.agreement.contract_info.ma":"{plan_name} is a Medicare Advantage plan and has a contract with the Federal government. I will need to keep my Medicare Parts A and B. I can be in only one Medicare Advantage plan at a time, and I understand that my enrollment in this plan will automatically end my enrollment in another Medicare health plan or prescription drug plan. It is my responsibility to inform you of any prescription drug coverage that I have or may get in the future.  Enrollment in this plan is generally for the entire year. Once I enroll, I may leave this plan or make changes only at certain times of the year when an enrollment period is available (Example: October 15 – December 7 of every year), or under certain special circumstances.","enroll_form.agreement.contract_info.pdp":"{plan_name} is a Medicare drug plan and has a contract with the Federal government. I understand that this prescription drug coverage is in addition to my coverage under Medicare; therefore, I will need to keep my Medicare Part A or Part B coverage. It is my responsibility to inform {plan_name} of any prescription drug coverage that I have or may get in the future. I can only be in one Medicare prescription drug plan at a time – if I am currently in a Medicare Prescription Drug Plan, my enrollment in {plan_name} will end that enrollment. Enrollment in this plan is generally for the entire year. Once I enroll, I may leave this plan or make changes if an enrollment period is available, generally during the Annual Enrollment Period (October 15 – December 7), unless I qualify for certain special circumstances.","enroll_form.agreement.contract_info.pffs.provider_info":"Before seeing a provider, I should verify that the provider will accept {plan_name} . I understand that my health care providers have the right to choose whether to accept {plan_name}’s payment terms and conditions every time I see them. I understand that if my provider doesn’t accept {plan_name} , I will need to find another provider that will.","enroll_form.agreement.get_all_health_care_from_plan":'I understand that beginning on the date coverage begins, I must get all of my health care from {plan_name} except for emergency or urgently needed services or out-of-area dialysis services.  Services authorized by and other services contained in my Evidence of Coverage document (also known as a member contract or subscriber agreement) will be covered. Without authorization, <strong class="ds-u-text-transform--uppercase ds-u-font-weight--normal">NEITHER MEDICARE NOR  <span class="ds-u-text-transform--capitalize">{plan_name}</span> WILL PAY FOR THE SERVICES.</strong>',"enroll_form.agreement.i_am_authorized_to_act_on_behalf":"I am the person authorized to act on behalf of the individual listed on this enrollment form under the laws of the state where the individual resides.","enroll_form.agreement.i_am_person_on_enrollment_form":"I am the person listed on this enrollment form or I am simply helping to complete this enrollment form.","enroll_form.agreement.i_have_read_and_agree":"I've read and agree to these statements.","enroll_form.agreement.late_enrollment_penalty":"I understand that if I leave this plan and don’t have or get other Medicare prescription drug coverage or creditable prescription drug coverage (as good as Medicare’s), I may have to pay a late enrollment penalty in addition to my premium for Medicare prescription drug coverage in the future.","enroll_form.agreement.pffs.info":"{plan_name} is a Medicare Private Fee-For-Service plan and has a contract with the Federal government. I will need to keep my Medicare Parts A and B. I understand that this plan is a Medicare Advantage Private-Fee-For-Service plan and I can be in only one Medicare health plan at a time. I understand that my enrollment in this plan will automatically end my enrollment in another Medicare health plan. It is my responsibility to inform you of any prescription drug coverage that I have or may get in the future. Enrollment in this plan is generally for the entire year. Once I enroll, I may leave this plan or make changes only at certain times of the year if an enrollment period is available (Example: Annual Enrollment Period from October 15 – December 7 of every year), or under certain special circumstances.","enroll_form.agreement.pffs.pay_info":"As a Medicare Private Fee-For-Service plan, {plan_name} works differently than a Medicare supplement plan as well as other Medicare Advantage plans. {plan_name} pays instead of Medicare, and I will be responsible for the amounts that {plan_name} doesn’t cover, such as copayments and coinsurances. Original Medicare won’t pay for my health care while I am enrolled in {plan_name}.","enroll_form.agreement.please_read":"Please Read and Sign Below","enroll_form.agreement.release_of_information":"Release of Information:","enroll_form.agreement.release_of_information_acknowledgement":"By joining this {plan_type}, I acknowledge that  {plan_name} will release my information to Medicare and other plans as is necessary for treatment, payment and health care operations. I also acknowledge that  {plan_name} will release my information including my prescription drug event data to Medicare, who may release it for research and other purposes which follow all applicable Federal statutes and regulations. The information on this enrollment form is correct to the best of my knowledge. I understand that if I intentionally provide false information on this form, I will be disenrolled from the plan. ","enroll_form.agreement.sales_agent_disclaimer":"I understand that if I am getting assistance from a sales agent, broker, or other individual employed by or contracted with {plan_name}, he/she may be paid based on my enrollment in {plan_name}. Counseling services may be available in my state to provide advice concerning Medicare supplement insurance or other Medicare Advantage or Prescription Drug Plan options, medical assistance through the state Medicaid program, and the Medicare Savings Program.","enroll_form.agreement.select_relationship_statement":"Please select the statement below that best describes your relationship to the person with Medicare listed on this enrollment form.","enroll_form.agreement.service_area_info":"{plan_name} serves a specific service area. If I move out of the area that {plan_name} serves, I need to notify the plan so I can disenroll and find a new plan in my new area. Once I am a member of {plan_name}, I have the right to appeal plan decisions about payment or services if I disagree. I will read the documents that {plan_name} sends to me when I get them to know which rules I must follow in order to get coverage with this Medicare Advantage plan. I understand that people with Medicare aren’t usually covered under Medicare while out of the country except for limited coverage near the U.S. border. ","enroll_form.agreement.service_area_info.pdp":"{plan_name} serves a specific service area. If I move out of the area that {plan_name} serves, I need to notify the plan so I can disenroll and find a new plan in my new area. I understand that I must use network pharmacies except in an emergency when I cannot reasonably use {plan_name} network pharmacies. Once I am a member of {plan_name}, I have the right to appeal plan decisions about payment or services if I disagree. I will read the Evidence of Coverage document from {plan_name} when I get it to know which rules I must follow to get coverage.","enroll_form.agreement.signature_disclaimer":"I understand that my signature (or the signature of the person authorized to act on my behalf under the laws of the state where I live) on this application means that I have read and understand the contents of this application. If signed by an authorized individual (as described above), this signature certifies that 1) this person is authorized under State law to complete this enrollment and 2) documentation of this authority is available upon request from Medicare.","enroll_form.also_chosen_medigap":"You've also chosen to view Medigap policies.","enroll_form.also_chosen_medigap_long":"You've also chosen to view Medicare Supplement Insurance (Medigap) policies.","enroll_form.are_you_enrolled_in_medicaid":"Are you enrolled in your state Medicaid program?","enroll_form.attention":"Attention:","enroll_form.authorized_representative.2025.address":"Address of authorized representative","enroll_form.authorized_representative.2025.name":"Name of authorized representative","enroll_form.authorized_representative.2025.phone":"Phone number of authorized representative","enroll_form.authorized_representative.name":"Name","enroll_form.authorized_representative.name.error":"Enter a first and last name.","enroll_form.authorized_representative.relationship":"Relationship to enrollee","enroll_form.authorized_representative.relationship.error":"Enter a relationship to enrollee.","enroll_form.authorized_representitive.name.error":"Enter a first and last name.","enroll_form.authorized_representitive.relationship":"Relationship to enrollee","enroll_form.authorized_representitive.relationship.error":"Enter a relationship to enrollee.","enroll_form.bill_me":"I want the plan to bill me each month.","enroll_form.check_box":"Check box to continue.","enroll_form.choose_sex":"Select an option.","enroll_form.choose_title":"Choose a title.","enroll_form.chosen_plan":"For {year}, you've chosen to enroll in {planName}.","enroll_form.city":"City","enroll_form.clicking_understand_disclaimer":'I understand that by clicking "I Understand" below means that I have read and understand the contents of this page.',"enroll_form.click_box":"Click box to continue.","enroll_form.click_button_to_choose_option":"Select an option.","enroll_form.complete_required":"Complete required information to continue.","enroll_form.cost_plan_enrollment_period":"Note: You can join a Cost Plan without drug coverage anytime the plan’s accepting new members. If you want to join a Cost Plan with drug coverage, you can only join during an enrollment period.","enroll_form.county":"County","enroll_form.coverage_loss_warning.fee_for_service.call_from_plan_representative":"Once your plan has your enrollment form, you will get a call from a plan representative.  This call is to make sure that you understand how a Private Fee-for-Service plan works and to confirm your intent to enroll in this plan.  If the plan isn’t able to reach you by telephone, then you will receive a letter by mail that contains similar information","enroll_form.coverage_loss_warning.fee_for_service.information":"Medicare Advantage Private Fee-for-Service plans work differently than Medicare supplement plans as well as other Medicare Advantage plans.  Your doctor or hospital is not required to agree to accept the plan's terms and conditions, and thus may choose not to treat you, exception in emergencies.  You should verify that your provider(s) will accept your plan before each visit. ","enroll_form.coverage_loss_warning.healthcare_from_employer_or_union_disclaimer":"If you currently have health coverage from an employer or union, joining {plan_name} could affect your employer or union health benefits.  You could lose your employer or union health coverage if you join this plan. Read the communications your employer or union sends you.  If you have questions, visit their website, or contact the office listed in their communications.  If there is no information on whom to contact, your benefits administrator or the office that answers questions about your coverage can help.","enroll_form.coverage_loss_warning.may_already_have_coverage":"If you are a member of a Medicare Advantage Plan (like an HMO or PPO), you may already have prescription drug coverage from your Medicare Advantage plan that will meet your needs.  By joining {plan_name} , your membership in your Medicare Advantage plan may end. This will affect both your doctor and hospital coverage as well as your prescription drug coverage. Read the information that your Medicare Advantage plan sends you and if you have questions, contact your Medicare Advantage plan. ","enroll_form.coverage_loss_warning.pragraph_2.pdp":"If you currently have health coverage from an employer or union, joining {plan_name} could affect your employer or union health benefits.  You could lose your employer or union health coverage if you join this prescription drug plan.  Read the communications your employer or union sends you. If you have questions, visit their website, or contact the office listed in their communications.  If there isn’t information on whom to contact, your benefits administrator or the office that answers questions about your coverage can help.","enroll_form.coverage_loss_warning.special_needs_plan.information":'This plan is a type of Medicare Advantage Plan called a "Special Needs Plan."  Special Needs Plans are designed to focus on the needs of people in particular situations.  If you want to enroll in this plan, you must meet its requirements. Some Special Needs Plans are designed for people who have certain chronic diseases or medical conditions and some are for people who have both Medicare and Medicaid.  Some are for people who live in an institution such as a nursing home (or need the level of care that is usually provided in a nursing home). To learn about the special focus of this Special Needs Plan and find out whether you meet the requirements to enroll in it, you must contact the plan directly',"enroll_form.cp_ma_type.label":"Cost plan without drug coverage","enroll_form.cp_pd_type.label":"Cost plan with drug coverage","enroll_form.deduct_from_check":"Deduct it from my Social Security or Railroad Retirement Board (RRB) benefit check","enroll_form.deduct_from_social_or_rail":"Deduct it from my Social Security or Railroad Retirement Board (RRB) benefit each month.","enroll_form.different_mailing_address":"Is your mailing address different from the address where you live?","enroll_form.do_not_pay":'<b>DO NOT</b> pay {plan_name} the Part <span role="text" aria-label="Dee">D</span>-IRMAA.',"enroll_form.email":"Email address","enroll_form.emergency_contact":"Emergency contact","enroll_form.enrolled.after_ten_days":"After 10 days, call the plan if you haven’t heard from them about your application. You’ll need the confirmation number listed above when you talk to the plan.","enroll_form.enrolled.all_set":"You’re all set. Your application is with the plan.","enroll_form.enrolled.call_plan_with_questions":"If you have questions, call your plan directly.","enroll_form.enrolled.confirmation_number_disclaimer":"Keep this number. You’ll need it if you contact the plan before your coverage starts.","enroll_form.enrolled.confirmation_number_for_application":"Confirmation number for your application:","enroll_form.enrolled.contact_directly":"Please contact the plan directly with any additional questions.","enroll_form.enrolled.contact_plan_with_questions":"Contact the plan directly if you have any questions.","enroll_form.enrolled.details":"<b> It will take at least 10 days before you'll see your enrollment in your account. </b> <p> If you don't see it after 10 days or you haven't heard from your plan, call your plan to ask about the status of your enrollment. If any of the required information on your enrollment form is missing or doesn’t match your Medicare record, the plan may contact you to get the missing or correct information. This could delay the plan's ability to process your enrollment. </p><p> If the plan determines that your enrollment meets all of the Medicare requirements and is complete, here are some important things to expect when your coverage becomes effective. This information is especially important if you enrolled late in the month, and you haven’t received a letter or your membership card by the day your coverage starts. <ul> <li> After the plan processes your application, you should get a letter from your new plan. This may take several days. If you don’t hear from the plan in about 10 calendar days, contact the plan to check your enrollment status. </li><li> Enrollment can be effective as early as the first of the next month depending on your circumstances. Your plan will give you your enrollment effective date. </li><li> If you need to fill a prescription before you get your plan membership card, let your pharmacist know your plan name and show any of these materials as proof of membership: </li><li class='ds-u-margin-left--4'> Your plan acknowledgement, welcome, or confirmation letter. If you haven’t gotten a letter yet, you might have a copy of an enrollment application signed by a plan representative. </li><li class='ds-u-margin-left--4'> The plan’s enrollment confirmation number. This is a different number from the confirmation number you got from this website. <b> You can’t use the website confirmation number as proof of plan membership at your local pharmacy </b> </li><li> If you have both Medicare and Medicaid, you should bring proof of enrollment in both programs, like your Medicare and Medicaid cards, a copy of a Medicare Summary Notice, a recent Medicaid bill, or a copy of your current Medicaid award letter. </li><li> If you qualify for Extra Help (the low-income subsidy), you can also bring proof that you qualify, like a copy of your yellow or green automatic enrollment letter from Medicare (if you automatically qualify) or your approval letter from Social Security (if you applied and qualify). </li><li> As a last resort, if you pay out-of-pocket for your prescription, save your receipts and work with your plan to be reimbursed. </li><li>If you have questions, call the plan’s toll-free number.</li></ul> </p>","enroll_form.enrolled.fill_prescription_before_card":"If you need to fill a prescription before you get your plan member card:","enroll_form.enrolled.fill_prescription_before_card_steps":`<li>Tell the pharmacy your new plan’s name and bring proof that your application was approved, like a welcome letter from the plan.</li>
<li>If you have both Medicare and Medicaid: Bring your Medicare card (or Medicare Number) and your Medicaid card or recent letter from the state about your Medicaid benefits.</li>
<li>If you get Extra Help paying for drugs: Bring a copy of your yellow or green letter from Medicare or your approval letter from Social Security saying you qualify.</li>
