nt toward your deductible.","msa_plan.your_responsibility":"Your responsibility","msa_plan.your_responsibility_tooltip":"This is how much you’ll have to pay if you use all of your deposit to meet your deductible. If you use your deposit for drug costs or for services Medicare doesn’t cover, your responsibility cost will be higher.",na:G$,navigation_menu:V$,next:W$,no:K$,none:Q$,"ntm.alert.avoid_part_d_penalty.body.before_iep":`<p>If you’ve gone more than 63 days in a row without <tooltip_creditable_drug_coverage>creditable prescription drug coverage</tooltip_creditable_drug_coverage>, you may have to pay a late enrollment penalty until you turn 65. Join a Medicare drug plan <strong>within 3 months of your Medicare coverage start date</strong> to avoid paying the <link_part_d_lep>Part D late enrollment penalty</link_part_d_lep>.</p>

<p>If you get <tooltip_extra_help>Extra Help</tooltip_extra_help> with your drug costs, you won’t pay a late enrollment penalty when you join a Medicare drug plan. <link_extra_help>Learn more about Extra Help</link_extra_help>.</p>`,"ntm.alert.avoid_part_d_penalty.body.enrollment_iep":"If you join a Medicare drug plan after your Initial Enrollment Period ends, your monthly premium may include a <tooltip_part_d_lep>Part D late enrollment penalty</tooltip_part_d_lep>. If you get Extra Help with your drug costs, you won’t pay a penalty. <link_extra_help>Learn more about Extra Help</link_extra_help>.","ntm.alert.avoid_part_d_penalty.body.enrollment_sep":"If you lost <tooltip_creditable_drug_coverage>creditable prescription drug coverage</tooltip_creditable_drug_coverage> before {current_day_minus_sixty_three}, your drug plan’s monthly premium may include the <link_part_d_lep>Part D late enrollment penalty</link_part_d_lep>.","ntm.alert.avoid_part_d_penalty.body.generic":`<p>Join a Medicare drug plan <strong>within 63 days of losing </strong><tooltip_creditable_drug_coverage><strong>creditable prescription drug coverage</strong></tooltip_creditable_drug_coverage> to avoid paying the permanent <link_part_d_lep>Part D late enrollment penalty</link_part_d_lep>. There are some exceptions, like if you get <tooltip_extra_help>Extra Help</tooltip_extra_help> with your drug costs.</p>

<p><drawer_trigger_avoid_part_d_penalty>How can I avoid the Part D late enrollment penalty?</drawer_trigger_avoid_part_d_penalty></p>`,"ntm.alert.avoid_part_d_penalty.body.past_iep":`<p>Join a Medicare drug plan <strong>within 63 days of losing </strong><tooltip_creditable_drug_coverage><strong>creditable prescription drug coverage</strong></tooltip_creditable_drug_coverage> to avoid paying the <link_part_d_lep>Part D late enrollment penalty</link_part_d_lep>.</p>

<p>If you get <tooltip_extra_help>Extra Help</tooltip_extra_help> with your drug costs, you won’t pay a late enrollment penalty when you join a Medicare drug plan. <link_extra_help>Learn more about Extra Help</link_extra_help>.</p>`,"ntm.alert.avoid_part_d_penalty.body.within_iep":`<p>Join a Medicare drug plan before the end of your Initial Enrollment Period <strong>({iep_end_date})</strong> (based on your date of birth) to avoid paying the <link_part_d_lep>Part D late enrollment penalty</link_part_d_lep>.</p>

<p>If you get <tooltip_extra_help>Extra Help</tooltip_extra_help> with your drug costs, you won’t pay a late enrollment penalty when you join a Medicare drug plan. <link_extra_help>Learn more about Extra Help</link_extra_help>.</p>`,"ntm.alert.avoid_part_d_penalty.heading":"Avoid the Part D late enrollment penalty","ntm.alert.medigap.important_enrollment_period.anon":"You get a 6-month Medigap Open Enrollment Period that starts the first month you have Medicare Part B <strong>and</strong> you’re 65 or older. During this one-time enrollment period, insurance companies can’t deny you coverage or charge you more because of a pre-existing health problem. <learn_more>When should I buy Medigap?</learn_more>","ntm.alert.medigap.important_enrollment_period.header":"Important: Your Medigap Open Enrollment Period","ntm.alert.medigap.important_enrollment_period.li":"<strong>Your Medigap Open Enrollment Period ends 6 months after <start_date>your Part B start date</start_date></strong>. During this one-time enrollment period, insurance companies can’t deny you coverage or charge you more because of a pre-existing health problem. <learn_more>Learn more about Medigap.</learn_more>","ntm.alert.parts_ab_required.body.enrollment_sep_page":"You can explore the plans below, but you won’t be able to join one until you sign up for both Part A (Hospital Insurance) <strong>and</strong> Part B (Medical Insurance). <a>Check when to sign up</a>. ","ntm.alert.parts_ab_required.body.medigap":"You can explore the Medigap policies below, but you won’t be able to buy one until you sign up for both Part A (Hospital Insurance) <strong>and</strong> Part B (Medical Insurance). <a>Check when to sign up</a> for Part A & Part B.","ntm.alert.parts_ab_required.body.search_results_page":"You can explore the plans below, but you won’t be able to join one until you sign up for <ma>both</ma><pdp>either</pdp> Part A (Hospital Insurance) <strong><ma>and</ma><pdp>or</pdp></strong> Part B (Medical Insurance). <a>