edicare Part B {and} you're 65 or older. During this one-time enrollment period, you can buy any Medigap policy sold in your state, and an insurance company can't deny you coverage because of a pre-existing health problem.","ntm.help_drawer.avoid_part_d_penalty.items.one.content":`<p>Join a Medicare drug plan before the end of your Initial Enrollment Period <strong>({iep_end_date})</strong> (based on your date of birth).</p>

<p>If you get <tooltip_extra_help>Extra Help</tooltip_extra_help> with your drug costs, you won’t pay a late enrollment penalty when you join a Medicare drug plan. <link_extra_help>Learn more about Extra Help</link_extra_help>.</p>`,"ntm.help_drawer.avoid_part_d_penalty.items.one.heading":"When you’re first eligible","ntm.help_drawer.avoid_part_d_penalty.items.three.content":"<p>Join a Medicare drug plan within 3 months of your Medicare coverage start date. If you join a drug plan after you've had Medicare coverage for 3 months or more, you may pay a late enrollment penalty if you’ve gone more than 63 days in a row without creditable prescription drug coverage. You’ll have to pay the late enrollment penalty until you turn 65.</p>","ntm.help_drawer.avoid_part_d_penalty.items.three.heading":"If you have a qualifying disability","ntm.help_drawer.avoid_part_d_penalty.items.two.content":"<p>Join a Medicare drug plan within 63 days of losing <tooltip_creditable_drug_coverage>creditable prescription drug coverage.</tooltip_creditable_drug_coverage></p>","ntm.help_drawer.avoid_part_d_penalty.items.two.heading":"If you lose other creditable coverage","ntm.help_drawer.avoid_part_d_penalty.subheading":"There are 3 ways to avoid paying the Part <aria_label_dee>D</aria_label_dee> late enrollment penalty","ntm.original_medicare.tooltip":"A fee-for-service health insurance program that has 2 parts: Part A and Part B. You typically pay a portion of the costs for covered services as you get them. Under Original Medicare, you don't have coverage through a Medicare Advantage Plan or another type of Medicare health plan.","ntm.tooltip.creditable_prescription_drug_coverage.body":"Prescription drug coverage (for example, from an employer or union) that's expected to pay, on average, at least as much as Medicare's standard prescription drug coverage. People who have this kind of coverage when they become eligible for Medicare can generally keep that coverage without paying a penalty, if they decide to enroll in Medicare prescription drug coverage later.","ntm.tooltip.creditable_prescription_drug_coverage.heading":"Creditable prescription drug coverage","ntm.tooltip.extra_help.body":"A Medicare program to help people with limited income and resources pay Medicare prescription drug program costs, like premiums, deductibles, and coinsurance.","ntm.tooltip.extra_help.heading":"Extra help","ntm.tooltip.part_d_late_enrollment_penalty.body":"You’ll pay an extra 1% for each month you could have signed up for Part D, but didn’t, and didn’t have creditable drug coverage. We’ll add this penalty to your monthly Part D premium.","ntm.tooltip.part_d_late_enrollment_penalty.heading":"Part D late enrollment penalty","ntm.wizard.heading":"Interested in a Medicare health or drug plan?","ntm.wizard.q.coverage_ending_soon":"Is your current health insurance (or creditable drug coverage) ending soon?","ntm.wizard.q.coverage_ending_soon.reasons":"What are some reasons my current coverage might end?","ntm.wizard.q.creditable_coverage":'Do you currently have health insurance that includes "creditable" drug coverage?',"ntm.wizard.q.creditable_coverage.what_is_creditable_coverage":`What's "creditable" drug coverage?`,"ntm.wizard.q.disability":"Are you getting Social Security Disability Income (SSDI)?","ntm.wizard.q.disability.ssdi":"What does SSDI have to do with Medicare coverage?","ntm.wizard.q.dob":"What's your date of birth?","ntm.wizard.q.has_medicare_number":"Do you have a Medicare Number?","ntm.wizard.q.has_medicare_number.yes.content1":"Using your secure Medicare account makes it easier to preview and shop for plans.","ntm.wizard.q.has_medicare_number.yes.content2":"Log into (or create) your account.","ntm.wizard.resource.coverage_options.button_text":"Explore Coverage Choices","ntm.wizard.resource.coverage_options.content":"Understand your choices for how you get coverage and compare options.","ntm.wizard.resource.coverage_options.heading":"Explore coverage options",