<ul>
<li>Chronic alcohol and other dependence</li>
<li>Certain autoimmune disorders</li>
<li>Cancer (excluding pre-cancer conditions)</li>
<li>Certain cardiovascular disorders</li>
<li>Chronic heart failure</li>
<li>Dementia</li>
<li>Diabetes mellitus</li>
<li>End-stage liver disease</li>
<li>End-Stage Renal Disease (ESRD) requiring dialysis (any mode of dialysis)</li>
<li>Certain severe hematologic disorders</li>
<li>HIV/AIDS</li>
<li>Certain chronic lung disorders</li>
<li>Certain chronic and disabling mental health conditions</li>
<li>Certain neurologic disorders</li>
<li>Stroke</li>
</ul>
<p>Check with the plan you’re interested in for a list of its qualifying chronic conditions. If you were recently diagnosed with a chronic condition that qualifies you for a plan’s C-SNP, you might get a Special Enrollment Period to join that plan at any time.</p>`,"plan_card.does_not_include":"Doesn't include","plan_card.does_not_include_drugs":"Doesn't include drug coverage","plan_card.does_not_include_health_costs":"Doesn't include: Health costs","plan_card.dsnp":"Who can join a D-SNP?","plan_card.dsnp.help_drawer":`<p>To join a D-SNP, you must be eligible for Medicare and have either full or partial Medicaid coverage.</p>
<p><strong>Full Medicaid benefits:</strong> Some plans may require applicants to have full Medicaid benefits, meaning they qualify for the full range of Medicaid benefits their state offers.</p>
<p><strong>Partial Medicaid benefits:</strong> Other plans may accept members who get partial Medicaid benefits, like help from a Medicare Savings Program. This usually means they get some help with their Medicare costs, but don’t get full Medicaid benefits.</p>
<p>Check with the plan to find out if you need full or partial Medicaid coverage to join.</p>`,"plan_card.enroll":"Enroll","plan_card.enroll_in":"Enroll in","plan_card.includes_drugs":"Includes drug coverage","plan_card.isnp":"Who can join an I-SNP?","plan_card.isnp.help_drawer":`<p>To join an I-SNP, you must live (or expect to live) in a facility that offers long-term health care services for at least 90 days in a row. Eligible facilities include:</p>
<ul>
<li>Nursing home</li>
<li>Intermediate care facility</li>
<li>Skilled nursing facility</li>
<li>Rehabilitation hospital</li>
<li>Long-term care hospital</li>
<li>Swing-bed hospital</li>
<li>Psychiatric hospital</li>
<li>Other facilities that offer similar long-term, health care services and whose residents have similar needs and health care status as residents of the facilities listed above</li>
